    "created_at": "2025-06-29T06:44:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-29T06:44:46Z",
    "body": "I couldn't find an actual \"documentation\" about that wording, but it seems it was in the [first version ever of Web Apps](https://web.archive.org/web/20041009144718/http://whatwg.org:80/specs/web-apps/current-work/#compositing) that introduced the canvas 2D API (I feel like I'm covered in dust digging this up). At that time there was a sentence stating:\n\n> All drawing operations are affected by the global compositing attributes, [globalAlpha](https://web.archive.org/web/20041009144718/http://whatwg.org:80/specs/web-apps/current-work/#globalalpha) and [globalCompositeOperation](https://web.archive.org/web/20041009144718/http://whatwg.org:80/specs/web-apps/current-work/#globalcompositeoperation).\n\nSo I guess the idea was that since these do affect *all* drawing ops, they're \"global\".  \n[This mailing thread](https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-whatwg-archive/2012Mar/0289.html) also had the same argument for `imageSmoothingEnabled` at the time it was thought it could apply to all drawings, though it ended up affecting only `drawImage` and `CanvasPattern`.",
